      "rev_n_4_cb3cc6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_cb3cc6_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_cb3cc6",
        "thought_text": "The current approach iterates through all prefixes and checks if their reverse is a suffix. However, it might not correctly handle cases where the longest palindrome is not simply a prefix or suffix but a combination of both. We need to ensure that we are checking all possible palindromic combinations of prefixes and suffixes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3068562775902388892",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406355.93646
      },
      "rev_n_5_089981_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_089981_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_089981",
        "thought_text": "Consider using dynamic programming to build a table that keeps track of the longest palindromic substring that can be formed by combining prefixes and suffixes. This approach would allow us to efficiently find the longest palindrome without missing any potential combinations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3068562775902388892",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406355.9364889
      },
      "rev_n_6_ab61e0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_ab61e0_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_ab61e0",
        "thought_text": "Another strategy could involve expanding around potential centers of the palindrome within the string. For each character (and between each pair of characters), try to expand outwards as long as the substring remains a palindrome. This method ensures that we explore all possible palindromic structures within the string.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3068562775902388892",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406355.9365
      },
      "rev_n_7_360b1b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_360b1b_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_360b1b",
        "thought_text": "The current implementation checks for palindromic subsequences that are both prefixes and suffixes but does not correctly handle the overlap condition where the palindrome can split into two parts, one being a prefix and the other a suffix. We need to ensure that the palindrome found is indeed a valid split of the string into a prefix and a suffix.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3233489143711336",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406388.97038
      },
      "rev_n_8_95002e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_95002e_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_95002e",
        "thought_text": "Instead of checking for palindromic subsequences, consider using a two-pointer technique to expand around potential centers of palindromes within the string. This could help in identifying the longest palindromic substring that can be split into a prefix and a suffix more effectively.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3233489143711336",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794406388.970453
      },
      "rev_n_9_3fecaa_0": {
